      "evidence": "template/scripts/_platform_common.py: in `classify_task_base_currency`, `generated_files(root, main_sha)` is called only inside the `merged.returncode == 1` branch after `conflicted` is non-empty. The tests are named `test_malformed_declaration_at_main_fails_explicitly_for_a_conflict` and `test_missing_check_configuration_at_main_fails_explicitly_for_a_conflict`, so they cover only the conflict path. The spec text (\"a malformed declaration SHALL fail explicitly\") and the agent-workflow.md paragraph don't say the error appears only when a conflict occurs.",
      "id": "declaration-validated-only-on-conflict",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The spec and docs say a malformed declaration, a missing `paths.checks`, or a missing file at main \"fails explicitly\". The implementation reads the declaration only when the trial merge exits 1 with named conflicts. On a clean merge it is never read or validated, so the gate passes despite a malformed or missing declaration at main."
